{
  "recordedFrom": "HEAD 05f22c14794e34d62c0fa861181c18e37aad4395",
  "note": "The cells whose decision the destination-aware gate intentionally changes, with the recorded HEAD action and the new action. tests/parity.test.ts asserts exactly these cells change and no others. This fixture's topology is the single-remote clone the golden file models; the cells a real two-remote clone (origin = personal fork, upstream = organization repository) changes are declared separately in tests/fixtures/parity-two-remote.json.",
  "rationale": {
    "bare-push": "A bare `git push` (and `git push origin` with no refspec) is resolved through git's own default push remote and the current branch, so it is a pushMain on `main` rather than the pushBranch its lack of a refspec suggested.",
    "head-ref": "`HEAD` resolves to the checked-out branch, so `git push origin HEAD` on `main` is a pushMain.",
    "unresolved-remote": "The first positional after `git push` is the repository. A token that is neither a URL nor a configured remote leaves the destination unresolved, so a governed write is denied rather than allowed as an out-of-scope URL.",
    "admin-verb": "A gh verb with no precise capability (`pr comment`, `repo delete`, `release create`, `workflow run`) is a conservative `admin` write, denied below `full` instead of allowed at every level.",
    "personal-fork-push": "The clone's own fork of a governed repository is the governed destination at the roster level, so its default branch is denied; this replaces the previous out-of-scope-by-URL allowance.",
    "personal-fork-auth": "A destination owned by the personal account uses that account's ambient authentication, so the gate does not mint an organization App token for it; the command still passes.",
    "compound": "A compound command that contains a governed write is an unsupported shape, so the whole command is denied instead of decided by its first word.",
    "assignment-prefix": "A benign leading `NAME=value` assignment is skipped to find the program word, so the command is observed as the `git push` it runs and its capability applies.",
    "pr-ready": "`gh pr ready` and `gh pr ready --undo` are `openPr` operations, not the conservative `admin` fallback, so a ready-state change is granted at propose and above and denied below it. The `gh pr ready 1` cells are the ledger's record of that decision; the literal `gh api graphql` read cell declares no change because HEAD already allowed it, and it is present so the read classification stays covered.",
    "gh-host": "A compound command has no single resolved `gh` destination, so the gate passes it without injecting the organization App token."
  },
